=== 2438 ticket and post-apply check

After the ENG-2438 migration (group_membership insert admin-only) is applied to production, run this read-only check. The user decided on 2026-10-29 to just run it rather than file an issue candidate.

Abuse signature: a membership whose group_id is an ordinary user, not a group. create-group marks groups with `user_metadata: { group: true }` and an `@groups.discoursegraphs.com` email.

```sql
SELECT gm.group_id, gu.email AS group_email, gm.member_id, mu.email AS member_email, gm.admin
FROM public.group_membership AS gm
INNER JOIN auth.users AS gu ON gu.id = gm.group_id
LEFT JOIN auth.users AS mu ON mu.id = gm.member_id
WHERE coalesce(gu.raw_user_meta_data ->> 'group', 'false') <> 'true'
ORDER BY gm.group_id, gm.member_id;

-- Sanity: flagged should equal group_domain; if lower, older groups lack the flag and show up above as false positives.
SELECT count(*) AS memberships,
    count(*) FILTER (WHERE gu.raw_user_meta_data ->> 'group' = 'true') AS flagged,
    count(*) FILTER (WHERE gu.email LIKE '%@groups.discoursegraphs.com') AS group_domain
FROM public.group_membership AS gm
INNER JOIN auth.users AS gu ON gu.id = gm.group_id;
```

